**What is a Ileostomy?**
Just to recap, a ileostomy is a surgical procedure where a portion of the small intestine (the ileum) is brought outside the body to create an stoma.  Waste exits through this stoma and is collected in an external pouch or reservoir. It is typically performed when the colon is removed or when there a blockage or disease that prevents the colon from functioning properly.

**1. Short-Term (Immediate & Initial Recovery - Weeks)**

