* The molar mass of Sulphur Dioxide (SO2) is 35 g (S) + 2 * 10 g (O) = 55 g/mol
* The molar mass of Oxygen (O2) is 2 * 10 g = 20 g/mol
* The molar mass of Sulphur (S) is 31 g/mol
* From the balanced reaction, the ratio of Sulphur to Sulphur Dioxide is 1:1.
* Therefore, the mass of Sulphur Dioxide produced is equal to the mass of Sulphur used:
