5. Solubility and selectivity can be controlled by modifying parameters (e.g., pressure and temperature).  
6. The low polarity of carbon dioxide (the most common solvent) can be adjusted with cosolvents.  
7. Suitable for heat-sensitive compounds due to mild operating conditions.  
8. Environmentally friendly, as CO₂ is non-toxic and leaves no harmful residues.  

